00:12:02.970 --> 00:12:05.060
Haru, can I come in?

00:12:05.060 --> 00:12:06.310
What's up?

00:12:11.270 --> 00:12:11.930
Here.

00:12:11.930 --> 00:12:13.670
Good Luck Charm

00:12:17.270 --> 00:12:19.060
Thank you.

00:12:19.060 --> 00:12:21.890
I'll come cheer you on tomorrow.

00:12:22.930 --> 00:12:27.100
Oh, is it weird to cheer on cheerleaders?

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:30.890
No, that's what cheerleading is.

00:12:31.970 --> 00:12:40.470
For the performers, the audience, and everyone
there to feel like saying "Do your best!"

00:12:57.720 --> 00:13:01.640
Gentlemen, today we will leap before we look!

00:13:01.640 --> 00:13:03.520
You can't leap if you don't look!

00:13:03.520 --> 00:13:06.100
We will fight for justice!

00:13:06.100 --> 00:13:07.970
No, we won't!

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:10.180
We will go for broke!

00:13:10.180 --> 00:13:13.520
So don't break anything!

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:16.140
Stop, my stomach hurts!

00:13:17.220 --> 00:13:20.600
Chen's Japanese has really improved.

00:13:20.600 --> 00:13:23.060
<i>Is </i>improving, maybe.

00:13:27.660 --> 00:13:30.620
National Cheerleading Championship     Finals

00:13:32.810 --> 00:13:35.020
We've come so far.

00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:36.310
Yeah.

00:13:36.310 --> 00:13:37.890
Coach Takagi!

00:13:37.890 --> 00:13:40.930
Oh! Did you all just arrive now, too?

00:13:40.930 --> 00:13:43.220
Yes. We were just meeting up.

00:13:43.220 --> 00:13:47.020
I see. I'm looking forward
to your performance today.

00:13:47.020 --> 00:13:48.680
Thank you very much!

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:50.100
Please excuse us!

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:51.470
Excuse us!

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:53.270
Haru, let's go.

00:14:01.560 --> 00:14:02.350
Hey!

00:14:02.350 --> 00:14:03.930
Hm?

00:14:03.930 --> 00:14:05.720
Let's both do our best!

00:14:06.930 --> 00:14:09.770
Yeah, let's! See ya!

00:14:15.310 --> 00:14:18.060
Now all of Mizoguchi weeps for you.

00:14:18.060 --> 00:14:19.600
What're you talkin' about?

00:14:19.600 --> 00:14:21.100
<i>All </i>of you?!

00:14:25.430 --> 00:14:26.890
Hey!

00:14:26.890 --> 00:14:28.390
Domoto!

00:14:28.390 --> 00:14:30.810
Don't ignore me!

00:14:30.810 --> 00:14:34.060
You're, uh... Kanisaki?

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:39.470
It's <i>Hana</i>saki! Don't mess up
the name of a superstar!

00:14:39.470 --> 00:14:41.100
Sorry.

00:14:43.470 --> 00:14:47.180
Domoto, this is a coup d'état!

00:14:47.180 --> 00:14:49.020
Where'd you learn to say that?

00:14:49.020 --> 00:14:52.220
You shouldn't be using such difficult words!

00:14:52.220 --> 00:14:57.470
Hey now, are you saying you know
that Domoto is Sparks' Captain?

00:14:57.470 --> 00:15:00.060
Kindly crawl off, you crab!

00:15:00.060 --> 00:15:02.520
My name means "flower," not "crab"!

00:15:03.930 --> 00:15:07.520
Our routine is not a circus!

00:15:09.350 --> 00:15:16.020
Sho's self-reflection notebook had
"Domoto called us a circus" written in it.

00:15:16.020 --> 00:15:17.890
Chen, that's enough.

00:15:17.890 --> 00:15:19.850
It's not right!

00:15:19.850 --> 00:15:22.350
On the very first page of mine...

00:15:23.600 --> 00:15:25.270
You brought it here?!

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:30.220
It said "Be everyone's teammate!"

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:35.180
I spent a long time considerin'
what "teammate" meant.

00:15:35.180 --> 00:15:43.020
But now I finally understand. Teammates are the
people with whom you've overcome adversity!

00:15:48.720 --> 00:15:50.680
Well said!

00:15:50.680 --> 00:15:55.020
That's right. Today, we'll show 'em all!

00:15:55.020 --> 00:15:57.390
You'll see cheerleading
that makes everyone smile.

00:15:57.390 --> 00:15:58.720
Yeah!

00:16:01.640 --> 00:16:05.430
Sho, you're surrounded by such good teammates.

00:16:05.440 --> 00:16:06.730
<b>You're not alone,
so look straight ahead!</b>

00:16:06.730 --> 00:16:07.440
<b>You're not alone,
so look straight ahead!</b>

00:16:18.350 --> 00:16:22.970
Yes. I can finally show you our
routine with my head held high.

00:16:22.970 --> 00:16:25.560
Yeah, we'll see for ourselves.

00:16:25.560 --> 00:16:27.430
Zip it, crab.

00:16:27.430 --> 00:16:29.640
My name doesn't mean "crab," already!

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:39.850
Sakura just got here.

00:16:50.140 --> 00:16:51.850
Sakura.

00:16:59.060 --> 00:17:01.350
Huh? Who's that kid?

00:17:01.350 --> 00:17:03.850
That's my son.

00:17:03.850 --> 00:17:06.270
The three of us live together.

00:17:06.270 --> 00:17:10.680
Coach, you're... a mother?!

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:13.520
A mother... That's great.

00:17:24.020 --> 00:17:26.100
Kirari!

00:17:26.100 --> 00:17:27.600
--Ryuzo!
--Go for it!

00:17:27.600 --> 00:17:29.100
Do your best!

00:17:38.720 --> 00:17:40.770
Sis...

00:17:40.770 --> 00:17:47.060
And now, the National Cheerleading
Championship Finals will begin!

00:17:54.850 --> 00:17:56.930
How many left?

00:17:56.930 --> 00:17:58.970
We're after the next one.

00:17:58.970 --> 00:18:02.220
I've gotten kinda nervous.

00:18:02.220 --> 00:18:03.720
Me, too.

00:18:03.720 --> 00:18:04.850
Yeah.

00:18:04.850 --> 00:18:08.770
What's more nerve-wracking,
a first date or this?!

00:18:08.770 --> 00:18:11.970
A date isn't nearly this tense.

00:18:13.470 --> 00:18:16.930
Everybody with the Breakers, please come in!

00:18:16.930 --> 00:18:18.020
Right!

00:18:34.220 --> 00:18:36.310
Go, Sparks!

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:42.930
Guys.

00:18:48.060 --> 00:18:49.470
Smile!

00:18:49.470 --> 00:18:51.180
Kazu...

00:18:51.180 --> 00:18:55.060
Let's put a smile on the faces
of everybody watching!

00:19:00.640 --> 00:19:07.310
Now moving on to Entry number twelve,
the Breakers from Meishiin University!

00:19:07.310 --> 00:19:09.470
Let's do this, guys!

00:19:09.470 --> 00:19:14.720
An all-men's cheerleading
team formed one year ago.

00:19:18.310 --> 00:19:24.390
Go, fight, win! Let's go, Breakers!

00:19:28.720 --> 00:19:30.020
Ready!

00:19:41.950 --> 00:19:46.120
Show your true self!

00:19:42.850 --> 00:19:47.270
I always hid my true self
beneath famous quotations.

00:19:49.310 --> 00:19:54.600
We can understand each other
by revealing how we truly feel.

00:19:54.600 --> 00:19:55.810
So I should reveal myself as I am in my own words.

00:19:55.810 --> 00:19:58.550
I'm so embarrassed.

00:19:55.810 --> 00:19:58.550
So I should reveal myself as I am in my own words.

00:19:55.810 --> 00:19:58.550
You idiot! Try harder!

00:20:01.550 --> 00:20:02.470
Remove your blinders!

00:20:01.850 --> 00:20:04.100
You can say that again.

00:20:04.100 --> 00:20:07.100
It's why things went wrong during
practice for the school festival.

00:20:10.520 --> 00:20:14.020
Solitary single-mindedness gets you nowhere.

00:20:14.020 --> 00:20:19.600
I gotta be movin' forward with
open eyes and an open mind!

00:20:26.720 --> 00:20:29.350
The coach caught me out.

00:20:26.910 --> 00:20:28.370
Your rival is yourself!

00:20:31.720 --> 00:20:38.640
Why could <i>he </i>always do everything like that?
I felt so frustrated for so long.

00:20:38.640 --> 00:20:45.720
But he was the same way. And everyone
has conquered their own frustrations.

00:20:54.930 --> 00:20:58.060
So I have to conquer myself, too!

00:20:59.640 --> 00:21:00.970
Ha!

00:21:03.810 --> 00:21:04.600
Welcome!

00:21:04.600 --> 00:21:08.220
B-R-E-A-K-E-R-S!

00:21:09.220 --> 00:21:11.310
Go, Breakers!

00:21:11.310 --> 00:21:14.140
C'mon, fans! Follow us!

00:21:14.140 --> 00:21:17.020
Say black and yellow!

00:21:17.020 --> 00:21:20.350
You say black and yellow!

00:21:20.350 --> 00:21:27.560
Okay, let's go! Meishiin! Go for love and peace!

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:54.700
Be harder on yourself!

00:21:55.100 --> 00:21:55.720
Ready!

00:21:55.720 --> 00:22:00.970
I babied myself by thinking "I can't do it,
it's hopeless, this is impossible."

00:22:00.970 --> 00:22:07.180
I couldn't do it alone. I learned to
do it because I'm with all of them.

00:22:07.180 --> 00:22:10.560
My body benefits this team.

00:22:10.560 --> 00:22:15.180
It's for supporting them better than anyone else!

00:22:15.180 --> 00:22:15.890
It's for supporting them better than anyone else!

00:22:15.890 --> 00:22:20.600
Without Haru, I honestly couldn't have done anything.

00:22:16.850 --> 00:22:17.600
<b>BEAT      HARU!</b>

00:22:21.810 --> 00:22:24.600
I don't know if I've beaten him.

00:22:26.270 --> 00:22:26.430
I'd like to beat your cheerleading spirit someday, Haru!

00:22:26.430 --> 00:22:27.360
<b>Beat Haru! Beat Haru! Beat Haru!</b>

00:22:26.430 --> 00:22:32.680
I'd like to beat your cheerleading spirit someday, Haru!

00:22:27.360 --> 00:22:27.400
<b>Beat Haru! Beat Haru! Beat Haru!</b>

00:22:27.700 --> 00:22:28.610
<b>Beat Haru! Beat Haru! Beat Haru!</b>

00:22:32.680 --> 00:22:34.560
I can't beat Kazu.

00:22:33.290 --> 00:22:34.370
<b>BEAT     KAZU!</b>

00:22:34.560 --> 00:22:38.680
I felt like he saw right
through me when I thought that.

00:22:47.020 --> 00:22:52.640
But everyone's broken their expectations
and conquered themselves.

00:22:52.640 --> 00:22:55.140
We're the Breakers, after all.

00:22:59.100 --> 00:23:01.100
<b>BEAT     KAZU!
Break yourself! Beat yourself!</b>

00:22:59.100 --> 00:23:02.600
That's why I want to beat myself!

00:23:02.600 --> 00:23:05.100
Go, Breakers!

00:23:41.640 --> 00:23:43.980
Men's Cheerleading Club
Breakers
Now Recruiting!!

00:23:42.720 --> 00:23:47.520
We're the Breakers,
an all-men's Cheerleading Club!

00:23:47.520 --> 00:23:55.020
You there! Together, let's support
everyone and make them smile!

00:24:01.220 --> 00:24:03.310
Go, fight, win!

00:24:03.310 --> 00:24:07.140
We are the Breakers!

00:24:04.830 --> 00:24:09.920
Cheer Boys!!
